Subject: [RFC PATCH v3 0/6] mm/damon: add mTHP collapse and split control
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This series extends DAMON with mTHP collapse and split control based on
access patterns.  Collapse (patches 1-3) is ready; split (patches 4-6)
is RFC-stage for community design discussion.

Background
----------
DAMON provides data access monitoring but lacks proactive huge page
management.  khugepaged operates blindly (always collapse) and has no
split capability.  This series gives DAMON the ability to:

- Collapse small mTHPs back to PMD THPs in hot regions.
- Split cold PMD THPs into smaller mTHPs, reducing memory waste from
  partially-hot THPs.  Critical for tmpfs THP-backed KVM guest memory.

Data-driven design (ARM SPE on Kunpeng 920)
--------------------------------------------
Real profiling data drives the split threshold and signal filter:

  - 97% of THPs have <10% hot subpages -> clearly cold, split them
  - 1-2% have 10-30% -> borderline, tunable via hot_threshold
  - <1% have >30% -> genuinely hot, preserve

  Signal vs noise: raw SPE samples show scattered 1-2 hits across many
  subpages.  The heatmap uses a two-pass signal threshold (>= 1/10 of
  peak chunk access count) to filter noise before computing hot fraction.

Architecture
------------

  damos_va_collapse()                damos_va_mthp_split()
  -> damon_collapse_folio_range()    -> damon_spe_hot_fraction()
  -> collapse_huge_page()            -> hot_pct < hot_threshold?
       [anon only]                      -> split_folio_to_order()
                                         [anon + shmem]

Collapse (patches 1-3):
  Reuses existing DAMOS_COLLAPSE action.  target_order=0 preserves
  the existing madvise(MADV_COLLAPSE) path.  No external mmap lock.

Split (patches 4-6):
  New DAMOS_MTHP_SPLIT action with configurable hot_threshold (default
  30%, sysfs-tunable).  split_folio_to_order() supports both anon and
  shmem folios -- critical for tmpfs/KVM scenarios.

  When SPE heatmap data is unavailable (no CONFIG_DAMON_SPE, or
  PMD-mapped THPs without PTE access bits), the handler splits
  unconditionally -- DAMON access pattern filtering has already
  identified the region as cold.

SPE Feedback (patch 6, three-phase):
  Phase 2a -- PTE access bits via folio_walk (fallback).
  Phase 2b -- Userspace SPE daemon -> debugfs -> kernel rbtree (ready).
  Phase 2c -- Kernel-native ARM SPE event handler (future).

sysfs interface:
  /sys/kernel/mm/damon/admin/kdamonds/.../schemes/0/target_order
  /sys/kernel/mm/damon/admin/kdamonds/.../schemes/0/hot_threshold

Test Results (ARM64 VM, 256MB anon, 60s)
----------------------------------------
Collapse: nr_applied=10  sz_applied=69206016  AnonHugePages->67584kB
Split:    nr_applied=11  sz_applied=73400320  AnonHugePages->0kB (16KB mTHP)
Round-trip: AnonHugePages 67584->0->67584

Compilation: gcc 15.2.0, ARM64 native, zero warnings.

Known limitations
-----------------
- Collapse limited to anon; khugepaged mTHP support pending upstream.
- SPE hardware required for hot/cold detection; unconditional split
  without it.
- khugepaged may re-collapse DAMON-split THPs (ping-pong).

Wang Lian (6):
  mm/damon: add target_order field for DAMOS_COLLAPSE
  mm/khugepaged: add damon_collapse_folio_range() for external callers
  mm/damon/vaddr: implement mTHP-aware DAMOS_COLLAPSE handler
  mm/damon: introduce DAMOS_MTHP_SPLIT action and hot_threshold
  mm/damon/vaddr: implement DAMOS_MTHP_SPLIT handler
  mm/damon: add SPE feedback for sub-THP split decisions

